  "body": "This family home, held for over 40 years comes to the market offering a generous 1338m2 (more or less) of North facing land zoned Residential Mixed Housing Urban. A 1960s 3-4 bedroom home occupies the site and has potential to be renovated, extended or removed. Developers may decide to land bank and explore the options of tenanting the house during this period subject to Healthy Homes approval. \r\n\r\nThe contour of the land is gently sloping and surrounded by attractive foliage which could add a tranquil outlook to future dwellings. Godden Crescent is a popular location on Mission Bay's ridge with a quick stroll to Eastridge Shopping Mall, Mission Bay activity and the fantastic Bays beaches and cafes. Well serviced by nearby bus routes and close proximity to the CBD. \r\n\r\nZoned for popular Kohimarama School and Selwyn College, and potentially Baradene College.\r\n\r\nThis in an opportunity for developers to maximize the value of the land and benefit, owners have purchased and have realistic expectations.\r\n\r\nNow is a fantastic time to purchase so don't delay.\r\n\r\nContact John Howard for further information.\r\n\r\nSee interactive features for this property on barfoot.co.nz. Click the \"View office website\" link at the bottom of this page.",
